# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "Porta X {#x-gate}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"A porta X é uma rotação de $\\pi$ em torno do eixo $x$ da esfera de Bloch.\n"
"Aplicar a porta X a $|0\\rangle$ resulta em $|1\\rangle$, e aplicar a porta X a $|1\\rangle$ resulta em $|0\\rangle$; portanto, é uma operação similar à porta NOT clássica, também conhecida como inversão de bit. A representação matricial da porta X está abaixo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr "No IBM Quantum&reg;, o estado inicial é definido como $|0\\rangle$, então o circuito quântico acima em representação matricial é\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "A seguir, vamos rodar esse circuito usando um simulador de vetor de estado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr "O vetor coluna é exibido como vetor linha, com números complexos (a parte imaginária é indexada por $j$).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "Porta H {#h-gate}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the $x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr "A porta Hadamard é uma rotação de $\\pi$ em torno de um eixo a meio caminho entre os eixos $x$ e $z$ na esfera de Bloch. Aplicar a porta H a $|0\\rangle$ cria um estado de superposição como $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. A representação matricial da porta H está abaixo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Saída da célula de código anterior](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso é\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its own symbol:\n"
msgstr "Esse estado de superposição é tão comum e importante que recebe seu próprio símbolo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis (along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Ao aplicar a porta $H$ em $|0\\rangle$, criamos uma superposição de $|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$ onde a medição na base computacional (ao longo de z na esfera de Bloch) daria cada estado com probabilidades iguais.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "Estado $|-\\rangle$ {#rangle-state}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Você provavelmente já imaginou que existe um estado $|-\\rangle$ correspondente:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Para criar esse estado, aplique primeiro uma porta X para obter $|1\\rangle$, e depois aplique uma porta H.\n"

